    "notes": [
      "Offscreen Qt uses software rasterization; absolute drag latency is not comparable to a GPU desktop session. Compare the relative open/closed regression instead.",
      "The offscreen QFontDatabase has no font directory, so card text rasterization may be cheaper than on a desktop session.",
      "A cold switch resets the whole ThumbnailProvider generation before the sample; a warm switch reuses the warmed LRU.",
      "Batch switching is measured through batch_list.setCurrentRow, the user-visible path. `_on_batch_selected` only rebuilds cards and does not schedule `_request_visible_thumbnails`, so warm cached icons are not restored after a list click; this is why cold and warm batch numbers are close.",
      "Cross-batch `_navigate_to` was observed to leave the card list on the previous batch because `_refresh_batches` prefers the stale batch_list current item; it is therefore not used for batch switching here.",
      "Each drag sample is one synthetic mouse move plus one event loop turn; each drag moves the box by five screen pixels and releases it, which triggers the production card refresh."
    ]
  },
